# Testing

Keep tests lean and behavioral. Prefer one invariant per test. No exhaustive CRUD snapshots.

## Must-cover (backend)

- Gateway: unauthenticated `/internal/**` is rejected; valid JWT becomes `X-User-*` headers.
- Inventory: concurrent reserve cannot oversell; release restores `available`.
- Payment: the same Stripe event id processed twice is idempotent.
- Review: buyer without a qualifying order is rejected.

```java
// ✅ GOOD — invariant
assertThat(second.available()).isEqualTo(originalAvailable);

// ❌ BAD — assert every field of a large Mongo document
```

## Frontend

Zustand cart unit tests (add, qty, empty). Query hooks: mock `fetch`, assert cache key + error mapping.

Do not add Selenium/Playwright suites unless asked. Browser-verify UX flows instead (shop, checkout, admin).
